DB -> Hook -> Provider -> Context -> Component
	1. Use hooks to get DB state
	2. Use Providers to hold DB state
	3. Use Context(s) to retrieve Provider state

SEE: https://npmtrends.com/react-firebase-hooks-vs-reactfire

LINT: Streamline `useX(x: T | null | undefined)`, Error types.
LINT: Streamline `if (error) return <Alert severity="error">{error.toString()}</Alert>`

